# 696. Count Binary Substrings

#Leetcode Link: https://leetcode.com/problems/count-binary-substrings/description/?envType=daily-question&envId=2026-02-19

#Approach: 
The substring must have equal 0s and 1s and they must be grouped consecutively, so valid substrings can only occur between two adjacent groups like 000111 or 01.

This suggests we should first count lengths of consecutive character groups (e.g., 2,2,2,2).

Between every two adjacent groups, the number of valid substrings depends on how many pairs we can form.

The number of such substrings is limited by the smaller group, so we add min(prevGroup, currGroup).

Summing this for all adjacent groups gives the total count in O(n) time.


#solution:
/**
 * @param {string} s
 * @return {number}
 */
var countBinarySubstrings = function(s) {
    let n=s.length;
    let p=0;
    let c=1;
    let res=0;
    for(let i=1;i<n;i++){
        if(s[i]===s[i-1])c++;
        else{
            res+=Math.min(c,p);
            p=c;
            c=1;
        }
    }
    res+=Math.min(c,p);
    return res;
};
